#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Snapshots and per-participant success figures for the usability study.

    eval-run start --participant Q7M4
    eval-run checkpoint --task T1
    eval-run report --participant Q7M4 --observations beobachtung.csv

`start` records the verified starting state, `checkpoint` the state at the moment a task ends, and
`report` compares both against the target state and merges the written observation.

Why a snapshot per task and not one comparison at the end: a later correction, a demonstration of the
solution, or the T8 reset would overwrite what the participant actually achieved. A missing snapshot is
never silently replaced by a later state — the report marks the evidence as missing and asks for a
manual decision.

Nothing here writes to the application. Reads run in one REPEATABLE READ transaction so a snapshot is
internally consistent, and only the fields the criteria need leave the database: no password hashes, no
token values, no game states, no media.

Research data lands outside the repository, under eval/erhebungsdaten/<code>/.
"""

